[size=5]Description[/size]
Combat Text adds the enemy damage feedback the game leaves out. Hit a zombie and a small health bar appears above its head, hidden again once it is back to full health. Every hit and every fire tick spawns a floating number showing the health it actually lost, so you can tell how close a zombie is to dying and how much each attack is worth.

An armored zombie shows its armor as blue segments under the bar, one per plate, from the first hit. A segment empties as its plate breaks. The number is the real health lost, not the raw damage, so a hit that armor or resistance eats shows nothing.

[size=5]Main features[/size]
[list]
[*]A health bar above each damaged zombie, hidden while it is at full health and gone when it dies.
[*]A floating number for each hit and each fire tick, showing the health actually lost.
[*]Armor shown as blue segments under the bar, emptying as each plate breaks.
[*]Fire ticks merge into one number, so damage over time stays readable.
[*]Bars, numbers, number lifetime, and overlay size are all configurable.
[/list]

[size=5]Requirements[/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelaststandaftermath/mods/1]BepInEx for The Last Stand: Aftermath[/url]. Install it first.
[/list]

[size=5]Installation[/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelaststandaftermath/mods/1]BepInEx[/url] [i](if no other mods were installed before, start the game once so BepInEx finishes setup, then quit)[/i].
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path examples:
[list]
[*]Steam: [code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\The Last Stand Aftermath\BepInEx\plugins\CombatText.dll[/code]
[*]Epic: [code]C:\Program Files\Epic Games\The Last Stand Aftermath\BepInEx\plugins\CombatText.dll[/code]
[/list]
[*]Start the game. Hit a zombie and a health bar and a damage number appear.
[/list]

[size=5]Uninstall[/size]
Delete CombatText.dll from the BepInEx\plugins folder.

[size=5]Configuration[/size]
To change mod settings, edit [font=Courier New]BepInEx\config\com.ivmakk.tlsa.combattext.cfg[/font]. You can turn the bars or the numbers off, set how long a number stays on screen and how fire ticks merge, and scale the whole overlay. Edit the file, then restart the game to apply the change.

[size=5]Source and license[/size]
